NC Medicaid allows **up to 60 days of therapeutic leave per calendar year** for an eligible nursing facility resident, subject to specific conditions. No more than **15 consecutive therapeutic leave days** may be taken **without NC Medicaid approval**. [[Nursing Facilities](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/2b-1-nursing-facilities/download?attachment)] (effective Aug. 7, 2024; current per amendment check)

## Conditions that must be met

Under **Clinical Coverage Policy 2B-1, section 5.8**, therapeutic leave is allowed only if:

- the person is a **Medicaid-eligible resident** occupying a nursing facility bed **for which NC Medicaid is paying reimbursement**;
- the leave is **for therapeutic purposes only**;
- the leave is **ordered by the resident’s attending physician**;
- the **necessity for the leave is documented in the resident’s plan of care**; and
- the **therapeutic justification for each instance** of leave is entered in the **resident’s health record**. [[Nursing Facilities](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/2b-1-nursing-facilities/download?attachment)]

## Other important limits

Policy 2B-1 also says:

- the facility must **reserve the resident’s bed** during the therapeutic absence;
- the facility may not receive other Medicaid revenue for that resident besides the reimbursement for the reserved bed during the leave period;
- the facility is **not reimbursed** for therapeutic leave days that **exceed the legal limit**;
- the therapeutic justification is **subject to state review**;
- the facility must keep a **cumulative record** of therapeutic leave days and note the resident on the **midnight census** as on therapeutic leave; and
- therapeutic leave **does not apply** if the resident is away **to receive inpatient or nursing services elsewhere, or at a different level of care in the same facility, when Medicaid is paying for those services**. [[Nursing Facilities](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/2b-1-nursing-facilities/download?attachment)]

## Transportation

NC Medicaid states that transportation from the facility to the therapeutic leave site is **not considered an emergency**, so **ambulance service for that purpose is not reimbursed**. [[Nursing Facilities](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/2b-1-nursing-facilities/download?attachment)]

